This page lists public [[opinion poll]]s conducted for the [[2012 French presidential election]], which was held on 22 April 2012 with a run-off on 6 May 2012.

Unless otherwise noted, all polls listed below are compliant with the regulations of the national polling commission (''Commission nationale des sondages'') and utilize the [[quota sampling|quota method]].

== First round ==
Starting on 12 January 2012, [[Institut français d'opinion publique|Ifop]]-Fiducial published a "rolling" poll for ''[[Paris Match]]'' and [[Europe 1]] which is listed in the tables below as "Ifop-Fiducial" without an asterisk, while separate polls not conducted as part of the "rolling" poll are listed with an asterisk (*).<ref name="rolling">{{cite web|title=" La présidentielle en temps réel " avec le rolling Ifop – Paris Match – Europe 1 – Fiducial|url=http://www.ifop.fr/media/pressdocument/397-1-document_file.pdf|publisher=Ifop|date=11 January 2012|accessdate=24 February 2018|archive-date=24 February 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180224114632/http://www.ifop.fr/media/pressdocument/397-1-document_file.pdf|url-status=dead}}</ref> Polls conducted specifically for subsample data are listed with two asterisks (**).

The publication of first-round polls was prohibited after midnight on 20 April 2012.<ref name="silence">{{cite web|title=Communiqué du 20 avril 2012|url=https://www.commission-des-sondages.fr/hist/communiques/communique-sondages-elections-presidentielles-20avril2012.htm|publisher=Commission des sondages|date=20 April 2012|accessdate=24 February 2018}}</ref>

=== Graphical summary ===
The averages in the graphs below were constructed using polls listed below conducted by the eight major French pollsters. The graphs are smoothed 14-day weighted moving averages, using only the most recent poll conducted by any given pollster within that range (each poll weighted based on recency).

[[Jean-Pierre Chevènement]] of the [[Citizen and Republican Movement]] (MRC) withdrew his candidacy on 1 February 2012 after failing to secure significant support.<ref>{{cite news|author=Sylvia Zappi|title=Sans moyens ni soutiens, Chevènement a tenté son baroud d'honneur|url=https://www.lemonde.fr/election-presidentielle-2012/article/2012/02/01/sans-moyens-ni-soutiens-chevenement-a-tente-son-baroud-d-honneur_1637230_1471069.html|newspaper=Le Monde|date=1 February 2012|accessdate=24 February 2018}}</ref> [[Christine Boutin]] of the [[Christian Democratic Party (France)|Christian Democratic Party]] (PCD) renounced her candidacy on 13 February and announced her support for [[Nicolas Sarkozy]],<ref>{{cite news|author=Béatrice Houchard|title=Christine Boutin retire sa candidature|url=https://www.lefigaro.fr/politique/2012/02/13/01002-20120213ARTFIG00695-christine-boutin-retire-sa-candidature.php|newspaper=Le Figaro|date=13 February 2012|accessdate=24 February 2018}}</ref> as did [[Hervé Morin]] of the [[New Centre]] (NC) on 16 February,<ref>{{cite news|title=Présidentielle : Hervé Morin se retire et se rallie à Nicolas Sarkozy|url=https://www.sudouest.fr/2012/02/16/presidentielle-herve-morin-se-retire-et-se-rallie-a-nicolas-sarkozy-635285-4772.php|agency=Agence France-Presse|newspaper=Sud Ouest|date=16 February 2012|accessdate=24 February 2018}}</ref> followed by [[Frédéric Nihous]] for [[Hunting, Fishing, Nature and Traditions]] (CPNT) on 22 February.<ref>{{cite news|title=Nihous renonce à se présenter et soutient Sarkozy|url=http://www.rtl.fr/actu/politique/frederic-nihous-renonce-a-se-presenter-et-soutient-sarkozy-7744127144|publisher=RTL|date=22 February 2012|accessdate=24 February 2018|archive-date=24 February 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180224113136/http://www.rtl.fr/actu/politique/frederic-nihous-renonce-a-se-presenter-et-soutient-sarkozy-7744127144|url-status=dead}}</ref> On 15 March, [[Dominique de Villepin]] of [[République solidaire|United Republic]] (RS) announced that he would not secure enough sponsorships to become a candidate "barring a republican miracle", effectively ending his campaign,<ref>{{cite news|title="Sauf miracle", Dominique de Villepin ne sera pas candidat à la présidentielle|url=https://www.lemonde.fr/election-presidentielle-2012/article/2012/03/15/sauf-miracle-dominique-de-villepin-ne-sera-pas-candidat-a-la-presidentielle_1670310_1471069.html|agency=Agence France-Presse|newspaper=Le Monde|date=15 March 2012|accessdate=24 February 2018}}</ref> and [[Corinne Lepage]] of [[Cap21]] was absent from the official list of candidates published on 19 March, having also failed to secure at least 500 sponsorships.<ref>{{cite news|title=Dix candidats en lice pour l'élection présidentielle|url=https://www.leparisien.fr/election-presidentielle-2012/dix-candidats-qualifies-pour-l-election-presidentielle-19-03-2012-1913613.php|newspaper=Le Parisien|date=19 March 2012|accessdate=24 February 2018}}</ref>

